+/// How long a kept empty pooled block stays empty before it is freed even where it is its
+/// pool's last one ([`Pool::aged`], [`Memory::age_aged`]): the age the X9 kernel's per-client
+/// accounting calls old (its LIVE line's `old30s`), so the two layers agree on "old".
+/// [`KEPT_EMPTY_FOR`]'s leave-one rule keeps a working set's dip cheap and keeps the room
+/// [`keep_room`] made; this longer period returns the base a burst left behind — blocks
+/// nothing had placed in for minutes, counted against the client's budget until they go,
+/// which is what filled the A image's backboardd budget at 168 s.
+pub(super) const AGED_EMPTY_FOR: Duration = Duration::from_secs(30);
+
